Subject: vulkan: let GGML_VK_DISABLE_HOST_VISIBLE_VIDMEM reach UMA devices

PR #22930 ("vulkan: prefer host-visible memory buffers on UMA devices",
commit 32120c10e3, first shipped in build b9668) made the device->uma branch
of ggml_vk_create_buffer_device() request
{eDeviceLocal|eHostVisible|eHostCoherent} FIRST, ahead of bare eDeviceLocal.
ggml_vk_find_memory_properties returns every matching memory type and the
caller takes the first that allocates, so on an AMD APU under the Windows
proprietary driver a host-visible/GTT-backed type wins over the BIOS-carved
dedicated heap. The weights then live in pageable "shared" memory: GPU
dedicated collapses, the pagefile grows, and decode tok/s is UNCHANGED
(shared and dedicated are the same LPDDR5X at the same bandwidth), so the
failure is invisible to throughput monitoring.

Measured on a Ryzen AI Max+ 395 / Radeon 8060S (Strix Halo, gfx1151, 96 GB
BIOS carve, Windows AMD proprietary driver), same model and same flags across
three builds (Qwen3.8-27B-Q6_K + mmproj, 64K ctx, -ngl 99, --flash-attn 1):

  b9596   28.17 GB dedicated, Available 4714 MB, 12s load
  b9667   28.17 GB dedicated, Available 4685 MB, 12s load   (d5fb104293, pre-#22930)
  b9668    0.07 GB dedicated, Available  273 MB, 60s load   (32120c10e3, IS #22930)

b9667 and b9668 are 39 minutes and one commit apart. All three print an
identical device probe (Vulkan0, 114507 MiB total, 108782 MiB free), so this
is allocator placement, not device discovery.

The same ordering change also made GGML_VK_DISABLE_HOST_VISIBLE_VIDMEM
unreachable on every integrated GPU, because the uma branch is tested BEFORE
the disable_host_visible_vidmem branch. That is why setting the variable had
no observable effect on this hardware.

This patch does not revert #22930 and does not change any default. It makes
the existing environment variable do what its name says on UMA devices too:
when GGML_VK_DISABLE_HOST_VISIBLE_VIDMEM is set, prefer the dedicated heap and
keep the host-visible options as fallbacks.

Generated against tag b10867. Regenerate if the base moves.

